{
  "_comment": [
    "Reference hierarchy for tb_geo_location (CONTINENT -> REGION), based on the UN M49 geoscheme",
    "(https://unstats.un.org/unsd/methodology/m49/). The Americas are one continent (AME, as already",
    "used live) with the four M49 sub-regions; Sub-Saharan Africa is split into its M49 intermediate",
    "regions. Each region lists its member countries as ISO 3166-1 alpha-3 codes (= GADM GID_0), which",
    "NiFi step 8 uses to find the parent REGION of an imported country. Taiwan (TWN) and the GADM-only",
    "codes (XKO, XAD, XNC, XCA, XPI, XSP, XCL, Z01-Z09) are not in M49 and are assigned by geography.",
    "friendlyIds are looked up per type (REGION vs COUNTRY), so a region code equal to some ISO3 code",
    "(e.g. MAF) is not ambiguous.",
    "Seeded by scripts/seed_geolocation_reference_data.py (idempotent)."
  ],
